          {
            title: 'Teen Patti',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Teen Patti (तीन पत्ती), meaning "three cards" in Hindi, is a popular Indian vying game that combines elements of poker and bluffing. Also known as **Flash** or **Three Card Brag**, it is one of the most widely played card games in the Indian subcontinent. The game is traditionally played during festivals, especially Diwali, and has gained international recognition through online gaming platforms.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: India\nTime Period: Several centuries old, exact origins unknown\nEtymology: "Teen" means three and "Patti" means cards in Hindi\nAlternative Names: Flash, Flush, Three Card Brag (British equivalent)',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 3\nMaximum Players: 6 (can accommodate up to 10 with variations)\nOptimal Players: 4-7\nPartnerships: No, every player plays individually',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nBetting chips or cash\nA flat surface for dealing and pot placement',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards per Player: 3 cards face-down\nDealing Pattern: Clockwise, one card at a time\nDealer: Deals to all players including themselves\n--',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
